{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"reasoning","text":"**Diagnosing trap variable scope issue**\n\nThe cleanup trap runs at shell exit, so local variables from the function are undefined then, causing unbound variable errors. Using a trap on RETURN inside the function can keep locals in scope for cleanup, but RETURN traps need checking for portability and extdebug requirements."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"reasoning","text":"**Deciding to use global variables for cleanup trap**\n\nLocal variables vanish before the EXIT trap runs, so switching to global variables set before the trap ensures cleanup can access needed IDs reliably. I'll refactor to define global IDs upfront, have the cleanup function read these globals, and set the trap inside the function."}}
